1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,010
Bitter cold, almost dark:
the last evening of the year.

2
00:00:06,170 --> 00:00:09,823
A poor girl shuffled along
in her mother's big slippers.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,968
Carriages raced by; she lost
them, and went on barefoot.

4
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:16,570
Matches…

5
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:18,465
who will buy my matches?

6
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,113
No one had bought a single match.

7
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:26,217
Candles gleamed in the windows;
it smelled of roast goose.

8
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:31,230
She huddled in a corner,
afraid to go home to her father.

9
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:33,920
Her hands were numb.

10
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,613
If she dared strike just one…

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,080
How it blazed!

12
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:43,792
A warm iron stove seemed
to stand before her.

13
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,561
Then it went out.

14
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:52,943
A second: the wall became a veil,
and inside, a roast goose steamed.

15
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:57,283
It hopped down and waddled
toward her — then darkness.

16
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:03,458
A third: she sat beneath a
Christmas tree ablaze with candles.

17
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:05,390
Out it went.

18
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,930
The lights rose and became stars.
One fell.

19
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:11,614
Someone is dying.

20
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,370
Her grandmother,
the only one who had loved her,

21
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:19,770
had said: a falling star
is a soul going to God.

22
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:25,177
A fourth — and there stood
Grandmother, shining and kind.

23
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,080
Grandmother!

24
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,495
Take me with you!

25
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:33,665
She struck the whole bundle,
to keep her near.

26
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:37,980
Grandmother took her in
her arms, and they flew up,

27
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:41,880
where there is no cold,
no hunger, no fear.

28
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:49,202
At dawn she sat there still, rosy-cheeked
and smiling — frozen to death.

29
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,348
She wanted to warm herself.

30
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:58,628
No one knew the beautiful things she
had seen, or the joy she had gone to.

